1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
 So, now let's talk about guardrails in Amazon Bedrock.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:09,520
 So, guardrails allow you to control the interaction between your users and your foundation

3
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,520
 models.

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:15,840
 So, you can set up guardrails to filter, undesirable, and harmful content.

5
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:21,200
 For example, say we have Amazon Bedrock and we set up a guardrail to block any kind

6
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,040
 of food recipes.

7
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:27,880
 And the user is using your model and saying, "Hey, suggest me something to cook tonight."

8
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:32,560
 Then, Amazon Bedrock will respond, "Sorry, this is a restricted topic.

9
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:35,480
 This is because we have set up a guardrail to block this topic."

10
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:39,280
 Of course, maybe you don't want to block food recipes, but something a bit more relevant

11
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:40,680
 to your business.

12
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:46,440
 You can also use guardrails to remove any personally identifiable information or PII to make

13
00:00:46,440 --> 00:00:48,600
 sure that your users are safe.

14
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:52,120
 You can also enhance privacy and you can reduce hallucinations.

15
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:56,200
 We'll see what hallucinations are later on this course, but the idea is that you want to

16
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:02,040
 make sure that the answers are safe and sound and that they are not just invented of

17
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,040
 the block.

18
00:01:03,040 --> 00:01:04,920
 So, guardrails can help you with that.

19
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:08,800
 You can also create multiple guardrails and multiple level guardrails.

20
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:13,360
 And you can also monitor and analyze all the user inputs that will violate the guardrails

21
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:16,680
 to make sure that you have set the guardrails up properly.

22
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:17,680
 So, that's it.

23
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:19,200
 Just a short intro to the guardrail.

24
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,200
 I hope you liked it and I will see you in the next lecture.

